 {name:'Gmail',what:'Business email connects an incoming request to an ongoing conversation.',when:'Use it for customer requests, agreed next steps and formal follow-up.',connect:'An email can lead to a Calendar event, shared Drive files and a reply grounded in the same project.',question:'Do we need to keep sending the working file as an attachment?',answer:'A shared file link can keep people on one working version. Review permissions before sharing it.',try:'Find the original customer request',result:'The original request is the starting point: discuss the cloud migration plan next week.',source:'https://support.google.com/mail/'},
 {name:'Calendar',what:'A shared time-and-context layer: the event connects people, schedule, meeting access and relevant material.',when:'Use it to agree a time, invite the right people, reserve configured resources and establish recurring project meetings.',connect:'Start from an email; compare permitted availability; attach a Meet link and Drive document; return to the event for meeting context.',question:'Can we see every customer’s availability and automatically open every attachment?',answer:'No. Availability depends on sharing. File access is governed by Drive permissions. A proposed slot is not an accepted invitation.',try:'Build an event by exploring the controls',source:'https://support.google.com/calendar/answer/6294878'},
 {name:'Meet',what:'A place for a live conversation with the people invited to the discussion.',when:'Use it when questions, decisions and alignment need a real-time conversation.',connect:'The Calendar event can provide the link and materials. Meeting notes can continue into a document and project collaboration.',question:'Are Gemini meeting notes available with every license?',answer:'No. AI note-taking requires an eligible plan and applicable settings. Participants need appropriate notice; review generated notes for accuracy.',try:'Capture the meeting context',result:'Notes capture the on-premise workload, assessment need and downtime concern, with dependency, database-size and timeline questions still open.',source:'https://support.google.com/meet/answer/14754931'},
 {name:'Chat',what:'Quick communication with a person or a small conversation group.',when:'Use it for a short clarification, a quick update or a document request.',connect:'A message can contain a file link or lead to a project Space when the discussion becomes ongoing work.',question:'Does Chat mean messages automatically disappear?',answer:'No. “Quick context” describes the purpose, not a retention promise. Message history and retention depend on settings and organizational policies.',try:'Choose Chat or Space',source:'https://support.google.com/chat/answer/7664687'},
 {name:'Spaces',what:'A named collaboration area in Google Chat organized around a project, team, topic or initiative.',when:'Use it for ongoing decisions, updates, shared material and coordination involving several people.',connect:'Carry meeting context into discussions and link to shared project documents. New members can follow permitted history when history is retained and accessible.',question:'Does posting a file in a Space grant everyone access?',answer:'Do not assume that it does. Review file permissions and membership; retained message history also depends on settings.',try:'Choose Chat or Space',source:'https://support.google.com/chat/answer/7659784'},
 {name:'Drive',what:'A place to store, organize and share working files with explicit access controls.',when:'Use it when the project needs a known file location and clear ownership instead of scattered attachments.',connect:'Calendar, conversations and editors can point to the same working file. Shared drives, where available, support team-owned content.',question:'What happens if the person who owns a file leaves?',answer:'Ownership and offboarding need planning. Consider the right shared-drive structure and edition availability; do not rely on personal folders alone.',try:'Share the working link',result:'Share Assessment.xlsx with named collaborators and review access. The link points to the same working file.',source:'https://support.google.com/drive/'},
 {name:'Docs',what:'A shared writing surface for notes, proposals and decisions.',when:'Use it when people need to write, comment on or review the same document.',connect:'Meeting context can become a working document linked from the event or Space; the proposal can reuse agreed next steps.',question:'Does editing the notes automatically update the Calendar event?',answer:'No. Linked documents retain their own content; changes to notes and event details are not automatically mirrored.',try:'Add a next action to the proposal',result:'Next action added: agree an assessment workshop, confirm owners and validate open questions before a migration proposal.',source:'https://support.google.com/calendar/answer/6192039'},
 {name:'Sheets',what:'A shared spreadsheet for structured information, calculations and assessment tracking.',when:'Use it when several people maintain the same table or need a common view of updates.',connect:'Keep the project assessment in Drive, edit it collaboratively and link it from the event and Space.',question:'Can we work with an existing Excel file?',answer:'Supported Office files can be edited using Google editors. Conversion is another option; check compatibility and advanced features before relying on a complex workbook.',try:'Update one shared assessment',result:'Presales adds dependency mapping. The technical team flags database size for customer confirmation. Both inputs remain in the same working file.',source:'https://support.google.com/docs/answer/9406611'},
 {name:'Gemini',what:'AI assistance for drafting and summarizing, used with relevant permitted context.',when:'Use it to prepare a first draft, identify open questions or organize information you will review.',connect:'Here the selected meeting notes, assessment and proposal supply context for a summary and follow-up draft.',question:'Will it know every project file and always be correct?',answer:'No. Capabilities depend on product, plan, permissions, language and settings. Supply relevant context, inspect the output and verify against its sources.',try:'Summarize with project context',result:'Relevant context supports a grounded first draft. Confirm requirements and leave unknown database size and timeline as open questions.',source:'https://support.google.com/chat/answer/15345722'},
 {name:'Workspace Security',what:'Identity, file-sharing permissions and organization policies shape who can access work.',when:'Review these controls when onboarding people, sharing externally, using devices or handling sensitive content.',connect:'The same workflow needs appropriate event visibility, Space membership and Drive access. Advanced controls such as DLP or context-aware access depend on edition and configuration.',question:'Does this mean every file is automatically protected from every risk?',answer:'No. Controls require appropriate licensing, configuration, user practices and review. Start with the actual sharing and device requirements.',try:'Review a sharing decision',result:'Use named recipients and suitable viewer/editor roles for the assessment. Review external sharing policy; do not assume a meeting invitation grants document access.',source:'https://workspace.google.com/security/'}
